		{ type = "interact" },
	},
	hint = "Speak with the marshal who keeps watch over Goldshire.",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[From the crossroads town of {link:goldshire}Goldshire{/link}, Marshal Dughan commands the defense of {link:elwynn-forest}Elwynn Forest{/link}. His soldiers are too few for the task. Yet he must keep open the roads that bind the capital to its farms, its mills and its mines. Every recruit who leaves {link:northshire-abbey}Northshire Abbey{/link} passes through his hands, and he sends each one wherever the forest bleeds worst.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[Dughan is the face of a kingdom stretched to its limit. {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} has no king in the throne, no army near at hand, and only the loyalty of ordinary men and women to keep its peace. He does not complain of this. He simply does the work that remains.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Deeds",
			text = [=[• He holds {link:elwynn-forest}Elwynn{/link} with a handful of soldiers, spread between {link:goldshire}Goldshire{/link}, {link:westbrook-garrison}Westbrook Garrison{/link} and {link:eastvale-logging-camp}Eastvale{/link}.
• He sends scouts into the {link:fargodeep-mine}Fargodeep{/link} and {link:jasperlode-mine}Jasperlode{/link} mines, where the kobolds grow bolder each day.
• He places a bounty on the {link:gnolls}gnoll{/link} {link:hogger}Hogger{/link} and on the {link:riverpaw-gnolls}Riverpaw{/link} raiders of the southern border.
• He sends what aid he can to the forest's outlying posts, though he rarely has any to spare.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Unrecorded",
			text = [=[Little is written of Dughan's life before {link:goldshire}Goldshire{/link}. This entry records only what his deeds and his post reveal.]=],
		},
	},
	chapters = {
		{
			key = "the-recruits-of-northshire",
			title = "The Recruits of Northshire",
			hint = [=[Complete your training at Northshire and report to Goldshire.]=],
			unlock = {
				{ type = "quest", id = 54 },
			},
			text = [=[The recruits arrive bearing letters from {link:marshal-mcbride}Marshal McBride{/link}. Dughan has little time to greet them, for kobolds hold the mines, gnolls prowl the border and thieves haunt every road. He puts each newcomer to work within the hour.]=],
		},
		{
			key = "beneath-the-hills",
			title = "Beneath the Hills",
			hint = "Investigate the mines of Elwynn on the Marshal's behalf.",
			unlock = {
				{ type = "quest", id = 62 },
				{ type = "quest", id = 76 },
			},
			text = [=[The reports from {link:fargodeep-mine}Fargodeep{/link} and {link:jasperlode-mine}Jasperlode{/link} confirm what Dughan has feared. The kobolds are no longer a nuisance to be driven out with torches. They are spreading, and they are digging deeper than any honest miner ever dared.]=],
		},
		{
			key = "the-southern-border",
			title = "The Southern Border",
			hint = "Deal with the matter of Hogger.",
			unlock = {
				{ type = "quest", id = 176 },
			},
			text = [=[For a long time the tales of {link:hogger}Hogger{/link} were told as fireside stories. Dughan stopped treating them as stories when the dead began to come home from the southern farms.]=],
		},
		{
			key = "the-collector",
			title = "The Collector",
			hint = "Follow the stolen gold of the mines to its end.",
			unlock = {
				{ type = "quest", id = 147 },
			},
			text = [=[The gold dust stolen from the mines does not stay with the kobolds. It travels by hidden roads to a {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias{/link} agent known only as the Collector. When the Collector's ring is found, it bears the mark of the old {link:stonemasons-guild}Stonemasons' Guild{/link} of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}. Dughan understands then that the thieves of {link:elwynn-forest}Elwynn{/link} are no common bandits. They are the masons whom Stormwind betrayed.]=],
		},
	},
	mentions = {
